From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Erik Bourget <erik@ebourget.net>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 15:27:31 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: apple: t8132: Add the ISP_SYS power domain

The ISP_SYS power state register at PMGR offset 0x530 is the only one
in the PMGR block without a node. Describe it so boards can manage the
domain.

Leave it disabled by default, as t8112 does: a board enables it once it
has been checked on that hardware.

Signed-off-by: Erik Bourget <erik@ebourget.net>
(cherry picked from commit 50d89e75eb1804a9466cb64c4b5c3e21ba176bcb)
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5.5
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-pmgr.dtsi | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-pmgr.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-pmgr.dtsi
index 6fbf09e8f9..5e31d6ce69 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-pmgr.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-pmgr.dtsi
@@ -790,6 +790,15 @@
 		status = "disabled"; /* Locked, don't touch it */
 	};
 
+	ps_isp_sys: power-controller@530 {
+		compatible = "apple,t8132-pmgr-pwrstate", "apple,t8103-pmgr-pwrstate";
+		reg = <0x530 4>;
+		#power-domain-cells = <0>;
+		#reset-cells = <0>;
+		label = "isp_sys";
+		status = "disabled";
+	};
+
 	ps_ans: power-controller@538 {
 		compatible = "apple,t8132-pmgr-pwrstate", "apple,t8103-pmgr-pwrstate";
 		reg = <0x538 4>;
